      "side": 1,
      "message": "The allow_role_switch parameter is only used for the connection establishment:\n```\nThe Allow_Role_Switch parameter specifies if the local\ndevice accepts or rejects the request from the remote device to switch roles at\nconnection setup (in the Role parameter of the HCI_Accept_Connection_-\nRequest command) (before the local Controller returns an HCI_Connection_-\nComplete event)\n```\nOnce the connection is established, the link policy settings takes precedence.\nThe link policy setting is configured via the Write Default Link Policy Settings and Write Link Policy Settings commands.\n\nFor the Role Switch command, you do not need to check the link policy. However the Switch Role Request will be rejected by the peer if it configured the allow_switch role otherwise.",
